// ALLOWED-DRIFT: parser emits the full-table-scan warning for a WHERE clause with no partition-key predicate; the legacy regex full-scan rule requires a bare-word table name and silently no-ops on the `$table` placeholder, so it never warned here. Correct per the AWS spec / matches legacy on a real table name (parser stricter).

SELECT * FROM $table WHERE optional_field IS NOT NULL
